@startsalt
' Screen: Promote Capture to Dataset Modal
' User Stories:
'   - US-514: As a developer, I can promote a flagged capture into a dataset entry
'   - US-515: As a developer, I can edit the input and expected_output before saving
'   - US-516: As a developer, I can carry over tags and optionally mark as negative example

{
  <b>Promote to Dataset</b>                                             [✕]
  ==
  {
    <b>Source Capture:</b> <i>Refund edge case — SLA breach</i>
    ==
    <b>Target Dataset</b> <i>(required)</i>
    ^Customer Support QA                                                 ^
    <i>Entry will be added to the working version (not yet published).</i>
    --
    <b>Entry Key</b> <i>(auto-generated, editable)</i>
    "capture_2026_05_10_refund_sla_breach                               "
    ==
    <b>Input</b> <i>(editable)</i>
    {+
      "My order #ORD-88214 hasn't arrived and it's been 2 weeks. I paid  "
      "for express shipping which was guaranteed in 2 business days. This "
      "is completely unacceptable. I want a full refund AND compensation. "
    }
    ==
    <b>Expected Output</b> <i>(pre-filled with agent response — edit to ideal response)</i>
    {+
      "I understand your frustration. I can see the express shipping SLA  "
      "was not met. I'm processing a full refund including the order total "
      "and escalating to our resolutions team for compensation review.    "
    }
    ==
    <b>Tags</b> <i>(carried over from capture)</i>
    "billing ×" | "refund ×" | "edge_case ×" | "add tag..." |
    ==
    {
      [ ] <b>Mark as negative example</b>
          <i>Flags this entry as a known-bad response for contrast training / rubric calibration.</i>
    }
    ==
    {
      [Cancel] | [Promote to Dataset]
    }
  }
}
@endsalt
